question:
Given an integer \( n > 1 \), for a positive integer \( m \), let \( S_{m} = \{1, 2, \cdots, mn\} \). Suppose there exists a family of sets \(\mathscr{F}\) with \(|\mathscr{F}| = 2n\) that satisfies the following conditions:
1. Every set in the family \(\mathscr{F}\) is an \(m\)-element subset of \( S_{m} \);
2. Any two sets in the family \(\mathscr{F}\) have at most one common element;
3. Each element of \( S_{m} \) appears in exactly two sets in the family \(\mathscr{F}\).

Find the maximum value of \( m \).

Determine the condition on $m$ such that the equation \(x^4+2x^3+mx^2+2x+1=0\) has four different real roots. Choose the correct option:

(a) \(m<3\);
(b) \(m<2\);
(c) \(m<-6\);
(d) \(1<m<3\);
(e) \(-6<m<2\)

Evaluate the integral \( \frac{\pi^2}{10} \int_{-10}^{10} f(x) \cos{\pi x} \, dx \), where \( f(x) \) is defined on the interval \([-10,10]\) by
\[
f(x)=
\begin{cases}
x-\lfloor{x}\rfloor & \text{if} \ \lfloor{x}\rfloor \text{ is odd} \\
1+\lfloor{x}\rfloor-x & \text{if} \ \lfloor{x}\rfloor \text{ is even}
\end{cases}
\]

Suppose that $x$ is an integer that satisfies the following congruences: \begin{align*}
3+x &\equiv 2^2 \pmod{3^3} \\
5+x &\equiv 3^2 \pmod{5^3} \\
7+x &\equiv 5^2 \pmod{7^3}
\end{align*}What is the remainder when $x$ is divided by $105$?
